[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2776727447","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104975#issuecomment-2776727447","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104975","id":2776727447,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lgX-X","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T19:25:46Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T19:25:46Z","body":"Can you explain what the problem is, and how this fixes it? It is still not entirely clear to me from the attached issue. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2776727447/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2776907554","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104975#issuecomment-2776907554","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104975","id":2776907554,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lhD8i","user":{"login":"SlyZ1","id":40855494,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwODU1NDk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40855494?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1","html_url":"https://github.com/SlyZ1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T21:00:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T21:30:32Z","body":"> Can you explain what the problem is, and how this fixes it? It is still not entirely clear to me from the attached issue.\r\n\r\nThe issue is : whenever you use `InputMap.load_from_project_settings()` in a `@tools` script in godot, every `Action` related to the navigation scheme is removed (and maybe more).\r\n\r\n\r\n- Here is what I think I understood from degguging the issue: \r\n\r\n`InputMap::load_from_project_settings()` clears `input_map`, before assigning every `Action` that `ProjectSettings::get_singleton()` has. However, this seems to only contain the `Action` that are related to the UI, and nothing that has a name which starts with `\"spatial_editor/\"`, which is what's causing all the errors in the console. So it seems that the function forgets to remap the other inputs that are not related to `ProjectSettings`.\r\n\r\n- What I didn't understand:\r\n\r\nFirst, I don't know if only the `spatial_editor` things are missing in the `input_map` after that `clear()`, or if there is something else missing, as I only tested on the MRP.\r\nSecondly, I don't know whether the fact they are missing is because `ProjectSettings` do not have the `spatial_editor` actions while they should, or because the function should get the actions of something somewhere else.\r\n\r\n- How my PR was supposed to fix the issue:\r\n\r\nAs said in the issue, setting the navigation scheme in the editor settings back to Godot fixes the errors, until you refresh once again the 3d node scene. This is because changing the navigation scheme remaps all the `spatial_editor` actions needed in `input_map`, but reloading the scene reapplies the `@tools` script which calls `load_from_project_settings()`, and does not reapply the navigation scheme settings.\r\nAnd so I thought that whenever `load_from_project_settings()` is used, it should reload the navigation scheme settings, which works but kind of does some ugly spaghetti code and breaks compilation in export templates as I am not familiar at all with everything that's going on inside godot. \r\n\r\nBut now as I am writting this I realize that a good fix would be to make sure that everytime the scene is reloaded, the navigation scheme settings should be as well, regardless of whether `load_from_project_settings()` is being used or not.\r\n\r\nEdit: Actually, that last fix proposal sucks, as `load_from_project_settings()` could be called anytime, not only on reload, and break everything again. So I really don't know now, I only thought of separating `input_map` in different dictionnaries for the different types of input mapping (UI, viewport, etc), but that seems way too over complicated to me. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2776907554/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777042431","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104975#issuecomment-2777042431","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104975","id":2777042431,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lhk3_","user":{"login":"SlyZ1","id":40855494,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwODU1NDk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40855494?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1","html_url":"https://github.com/SlyZ1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SlyZ1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T21:56:47Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T21:56:47Z","body":"This doesn't entirely work, as loading the project values after the default ones results in trying to overwrite some of the default values in the `input_map`, which is not supported and causes errors","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777042431/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2777084681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104975#issuecomment-2777084681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104975","id":2777084681,"node_id":"